// [M-module-file-submodule-split-silent-orphan] repro fixture, head half.
//
// Head file of the file-submodule `module_file_orphan_repro.core` — the
// ONLY file in this directory whose OWN name matches the last segment of
// the module path (`core`). `resolve_module_paths` resolves a plain
// `import module_file_orphan_repro.core` to exactly this file.
//
// `scattered.nv` (its sibling in THIS SAME directory) declares the
// IDENTICAL `module module_file_orphan_repro.core` but is scattered
// directly beside this file instead of living in a dedicated `core/`
// folder-module (D78 "file OR folder") — this repros the historical
// `std/src/time/{duration,timestamp,monotonic}.nv` bug (fixed by moving
// those three files into `std/src/time/duration/`, Plan 211) at package
// scale. See `../module_file_orphan.nv` — the actual EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR
// test — for the E_MODULE_FILE_ORPHAN repro this pair exists to trigger.
//
// This file has no `test` blocks — `is_folder_module_dir` groups it with
// `scattered.nv` (identical declaration) as a library folder-module, which
// the test-runner's directory walk skips (`folder_module_has_tests` ==
// false) — neither file is ever compiled as a standalone entry; both are
// reachable only via explicit `import`.
module module_file_orphan_repro.core

export fn head_value() -> int => 1
